    {
      "entryId": "2sa-7-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God covenants with David that his seed will build a house and his throne will be established forever. Luke records the angel Gabriel announcing that Jesus will receive the throne of His father David and of His kingdom there will be no end. First principle: the kingdom is guaranteed by unconditional divine covenant sworn to David.",
      "density": 2.8286,
      "words": 56,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "2sa-23-5",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "David's last prophetic words declare that God has made with him an everlasting covenant, ordered in all things and sure, and He will make all his salvation to branch forth. First principle: the messianic covenant outlives all earthly failure and blossoms in Christ.",
      "density": 2.7893,
      "words": 43,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 30,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "2sa-7-14",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Father-son covenant with chastening rod included. First principle: the decree-sonship of Psalm 2 and the Davidic covenant are the same verse to Hebrews — and the chastening clause points to the cross.",
      "density": 2.2857,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 26,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "2sa-22-50",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The thanksgiving goes international. First principle: Romans 15 quotes David's resolve as proof of the Gentile plan — praise among the nations was the king's own mission statement.",
      "density": 2.0714,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "2sa-22-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The deliverance song David sings when the LORD delivered him from all enemies. First principle: the psalm of chapter 22 is Psalm 18 in place — the rescue-vocabulary of the king who trusted.",
      "density": 1.9679,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "2sa-12-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Confession one word long; pardon immediate. First principle: the psalms of forgiveness (32, 51) come out of this sentence — sin put away, death sentence lifted, consequences remaining.",
      "density": 1.9571,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "2sa-24-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "David intercedes at the plague-angel's sight: the shepherd offers himself for the sheep. First principle: the king's substitution instinct points to the greater Shepherd-King who does not pray it but performs it.",
      "density": 1.8857,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "2sa-7-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "House, kingdom, throne — forever before thee. First principle: the oath that outruns exile — Gabriel repeats it to Mary over the child in her womb.",
      "density": 1.7357,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "2sa-7-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The seed builds; the throne is established forever. First principle: Solomon builds the temple, but the verse outruns him — the forever-establishment is David's greater Son.",
